      "content": "PART A: CONCEPT OF INFLATION"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Inflation is broadly categorized into Demand-Pull and Cost-Push inflation.",
        "Speed-based inflation includes Creeping, Walking, Galloping, and Hyperinflation.",
        "Demand-side and supply-side factors drive structural price level changes in the economy.",
        "Monetary measures by the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) and Fiscal measures by the Government are used to manage inflation.",
        "Inflation significantly impacts economic growth, purchasing power, and different socio-economic classes."
      ],
